# URL dataset acquisition plan v1

## Purpose

Acquire the official UCSD malicious-URL SVM-light archive as recoverable, checkpoint-excluded material. Hash and safely inventory the entire archive, but extract only the first two chronological day files plus feature metadata for a bounded parser/protocol calibration.

## Source and storage

- Source: `https://www.sysnet.ucsd.edu/projects/url/url_svmlight.tar.gz`
- Archive destination: `.deps/url_dataset/url_svmlight.tar.gz`
- Extracted prefix: `.deps/url_dataset/prefix/`
- Persistent output: `sources/url_dataset_manifest_v1.json`
- Raw archive and extracted data remain under `.deps` and must not enter the checkpoint. The public page requests citation but no explicit redistribution license has been located, so no raw bytes will be redistributed.

## Safety and integrity

1. Download to an atomic `.part` file, streaming both bytes and SHA-256; reuse an already completed local archive after re-hashing it.
2. Reject archive members that are absolute, contain `..`, are links, devices, or other non-regular/non-directory types.
3. Record every member name and uncompressed size in the manifest.
4. Extract only members whose basenames are `Day0.svm`, `Day1.svm`, or `FeatureTypes`. Copy their streams to flat, atomically replaced files and hash them.
5. Fail if either day file is absent. Do not parse examples or run numerical learning in this acquisition task.

## Decision rule

Proceed to a separately preregistered numerical calibration only if the archive is safely readable and both chronological day files are pinned. Otherwise retain the failure and repair only the acquisition/parser boundary.
